SUMMARY:Collective Liberation: A BIPOC-Led Community Event
DESCRIPTION:Psychedelic Society of Asheville\nPlease join us on Saturday\,
  July 18\, 2026\, from 11:00 AM –1:00 PM at [Third Room](https://thirdro
 om.art/) in Asheville for **Collective Liberation: Subverting Segregation 
 Through The Psychedelic Healing Arts**.\n\nThis will be a meaningful gathe
 ring rooted in connection\, healing\, and collective possibility.\nWe're h
 onored to welcome [COHOBA](https://cohoba.org/)\, North Carolina's first p
 sychedelic-positive\, BIPOC-led nonprofit organization based out of Charol
 ette.\n\nCOHOBA’s work is transforming the landscape of wellness through
  mental health services\, somatic care\, creative expression\, and communi
 ty-centered healing. Grounded in the understanding that true wellness emer
 ges through relationship\, culture\, and collective care\, COHOBA is helpi
 ng reimagine what accessible and inclusive healing can look like.\n\nThis 
 special event is an opportunity to meet COHOBA co-founders [Laura Camilo](
 https://cohoba.org/our-team/)\, MSW\, LCSW\, and [Daniel De La Cruz](https
 ://cohoba.org/our-team/)\, MSW\, LCSW\, hear the inspiring story behind th
 eir work\, and engage in meaningful conversation with others who share a v
 ision for a more connected world.\n\nTogether\, we'll explore how communit
 ies can become powerful spaces for healing\, belonging\, and transformatio
 n. We'll reflect on expanding access to care\, fostering resilience\, and 
 creating more inclusive pathways for wellness and psychedelic education an
 d exploration.\n\nWhether you're deeply involved in this work or simply cu
 rious to learn more\, you'll find a welcoming space where lived experience
  is honored\, questions are encouraged\, and genuine connection can flouri
 sh.\n\nThis is a donation-based event\, with a suggested contribution of *
 *$15–$30**. No one will be turned away due to lack of funds. Please comp
 lete your registration and submit your donation via Venmo ([@psysocietyavl
 ](https://account.venmo.com/u/psysocietyavl))\, and include “COHOBA” i
 n the payment note. Your donation directly supports community-centered pro
 gramming\, accessible healing spaces\, and the continued growth of COHOBA'
 s mission and vision.\n\nCome be part of an afternoon of inspiration\, con
 nection\, and collective imagination. We look forward to gathering with yo
 u all in Asheville.
